@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# smallpt playground
+
+Kevin Beason's [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) C++ path tracer compiled to WebAssembly, with an entirely client-side interface in `index.html`.
+
+## Build
+
+Install Emscripten (`em++` must be on PATH), then run:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+```
+
+This produces `public/smallpt.js` and `public/smallpt.wasm`. Both artifacts are included, so rebuilding is only needed after modifying C++. Deploy the repository as static files over HTTP(S), with `.wasm` served as `application/wasm`. No application backend or special cross-origin isolation headers are required.
+
+## Implementation
+
+`src/smallpt.original.cpp` preserves the upstream source. `src/smallpt.cpp` retains the original Cornell box, intersections, diffuse/specular/dielectric materials, Monte Carlo radiance, and camera sampling; its CLI and PPM output are replaced by exported `setup` and `render_rows` functions. An explicit brace fixes the original ambiguous nested `if` warning without changing behavior. The worker calls these functions in row batches and transfers RGBA buffers to the canvas. A 1 MB stack accommodates recursive tracing.
+
+Rendering starts automatically. Randomize changes both sphere tints and side-wall colors; reset restores the original palette. Samples and resolution trigger a fresh render. PNG download exports the visible image. The initial `public/preview.png` was rendered from the same adapted C++ code at 256 spp, rather than being a substitute renderer. With `SMALLPT_PREVIEW` defined, a native build writes a PPM preview to `/tmp/smallpt-preview.ppm`.
+
+Original renderer © 2006–2008 Kevin Beason, MIT license. See `LICENSE.smallpt`.
+
+## Checks
+
+`npm run check` checks JavaScript syntax and executes the compiled WebAssembly in Node with a local binary loader. It verifies lit/opaque pixels, changed color output, and deterministic scene reset, without starting a server or opening a browser.
